{{!-- One row of the sidebar's Actors tab.

      Core's `templates/sidebar/partials/document-partial.hbs`, plus what a character plays. Every
      class, data attribute and action is core's and has to stay that way: the directory's click
      routing, drag handles, search filter and context menu all find the row through them, and the
      entry's context IS the Actor document, which is where `directoryNote` lives.

      Faded, after the name, on the same line. Which playbook someone plays is the first thing worth
      knowing off a list of six names — and the last thing worth a second line of row height on a
      tab you glance at. --}}
<li class="directory-item entry document {{ @root.documentCls }} flexrow" data-entry-id="{{ id }}">
    {{#if thumbnail}}
    <img class="thumbnail" src="{{ thumbnail }}" alt="{{ name }}" loading="lazy">
    {{/if}}
    <a class="entry-name ellipsis" data-action="activateEntry">{{ name }}</a>
    {{#if directoryNote}}
    <span class="stonetop-directory-note">{{ directoryNote }}</span>
    {{/if}}
</li>
